source "Kconfig.zephyr"

config ESC_DIAG
	bool "Run link diagnostics instead of the milestone 4a register check"
	default n
	help
	  Diagnostic build, used in place of the milestone 4a register check
	  when the ESC does not answer over SPI.

	  Tests the NSS wire by asserting chip select and watching for the
	  ESC's reaction on IRQ and MISO — NSS and SCK are ESC inputs, so a
	  pull-up cannot tell a carrying wire from a dead one, and this is the
	  only way to see them. Ends in a live monitor of every SPI line so
	  wiring can be poked at without reflashing.

config SERVO_LOCAL_SWEEP
	bool "Sweep the servo locally instead of following EtherCAT"
	default n
	help
	  Milestone 5a behaviour: ignore the bus and sweep the actuator from a
	  local counter. Proves the PWM channel, the actuator wiring and its
	  power supply on their own, so that if the angle later arrives over
	  EtherCAT and nothing moves, the mechanical half is already ruled out.

	  Leave this off for normal operation, where the angle comes from the
	  master as process data.
